{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792229972,"nonce":"J0jlICg5JFQJiK9larEV2Rnjvpg=","title":"Set difference skips the disjoint-kinds shortcut when the sets are typed set boxes","message":"zb_set_disjoint_kinds lets `r - ar` copy `r` without probing when `r` holds only sets and `ar` only tuples (nqueens' `place`). It tested every value of `r` for the library set's box kind (SET_TAG), so a set whose values are boxes of a typed frozenset shape (kinds in the keyed range) took the probing path: one zb_any_eq per value, through zb_hook_shaped_eq and zb_set_eq_any_s1.\n\nnqueens met it once `set(map(frozenset, poscols))` was typed (7270cdb): retired instructions for one trial went from 107G to 321G.\n\nFix: zb_set_all_sets, which accepts a value of the custom category whose kind is SET_TAG's or a keyed set's, replaces the SET_TAG test on both sides. nqueens one trial: 112G instructions (107G before the map rewrite).","files":null}]}